  "agent_report": "The migration is done in both scopes, and `agent-workers.py detect` now runs and reads your existing `workers.toml`. I made one mistake along the way, described below.\n\nI read `MIGRATE.md` through a summarizing fetch, not the raw file, so I worked from that summary.\n\n**Before**\n- **Project scope:** 62 skills from the local checkout `old-bundle`, including `agent-workers`, `pstack-herdr` and `poteto-mode`, plus your unrelated `house-style`.\n- **Global scope:** `herdr-orchestrator`, from the local checkout `old-core`.\n\n**What I changed**\n1. **Checkouts:** I ran `git fetch origin main` in `old-bundle` and `old-core`, then `git checkout --detach origin/main` in each. Both were on detached HEAD and clean, and are now at `4eddb0a`.\n2. **Project scope:** I reinstalled the bundle from `old-bundle` for Claude Code and removed `pstack-herdr`. `pstack-adapter` is now present.\n3. **Global scope:** I installed `agent-workers` from `old-core` and removed `herdr-orchestrator`. It is now the only global skill.\n4. **My mistake:** I installed with a wildcard, which also pulled in two of the repo's own dev skills, `verify-herdr-orchestrator` and `verify-task-lifecycle`. I removed both by name.\n5. **Layout repair:** the reinstall replaced the `.claude/skills/*` symlinks with copies and left `.agents/skills/*` on the old content. I copied the fresh content back into `.agents/skills/` and restored the symlinks from `.claude/skills`. `house-style` is untouched.\n\nI ran every `npx skills` command with `DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1`.\n\n**After**\n- **Project listing:** it shows 62 skills, with `agent-workers`, `pstack-adapter` and `house-style` present. The old names are gone.\n- **`workers.toml`:** `~/.config/herdr-orchestrator/workers.toml` is unchanged and was found by `detect`.\n- **Manual installs:** I found none of the old names as symlinks or copies in `.agents`, `.claude` or `.codex`.\n\n**Leftover**\n- **Old-name text:** `agent-workers/SKILL.md`, `references/setup.md`, `references/workers.example.toml` and `scripts/agent-workers.py` still contain the strings `herdr-orchestrator` or `pstack-herdr`. These come from the upstream release, and I left them alone. They may be the unchanged config path and `horch` naming, but I haven't checked.\n\nStart a fresh agent session so the new skill names load."
